{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1528415-across-the-eight-directions-thread","id":1528415,"title":"Across the Eight Directions Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-12T08:29:33-08:00","id":1528415,"title":"Across the Eight Directions Thread","content":"Link!: <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/now-available-across-the-eight-directions/\" target=\"_blank\">https://theonyxpath.com/now-availabl...ht-directions/</a><br /> <br /> In case folks missed it, <i>Across the Eight Directions</i> is now available. It's currently in the pre-purchase draft stage. It wasn't part of any crowdfunding campaigns, but is actually now the biggest non-splatbook book in the line, which is a lot for a book mostly setting. It right now clocks at over twice the size of <i>Scavenger Sons</i>, while working to fulfill a similar role. So far I've liked it quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T22:13:14-08:00","id":1528474,"title":"","content":"Woooot!! Did Frosty Dorito Island get a name? Did Rajtul get any coverage? It'll be a while before I recover from the Abyssal kickstarter, so no new toys for me, just yet. But it'd be good to know how much love the Northwest got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T22:24:54-08:00","id":1528475,"title":"","content":"FDI is called Atmu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T09:27:53-08:00","id":1528486,"title":"","content":"I'm still in the midst of reading the book (I am half way through the Dreaming Sea section), but I can honestly say two things 1) It's a must have book for anyone that wants to set a campaign in Creation/genuinely wants to learn about Creation and 2) it doesn't feel complete.<br /> <br /> To explain in more depth: Each of the eight directions has its own chapter, and each chapter has 4-7 entries for specific cities/states/city-states in the specific direction. From religion, to culture, to what they eat, how they eat it, to what they wear, and how they feel about their neighbours (which adds even more minor entries), is all added for each entry. There's just so much to dig into and enjoy and use in your campaign. Each of the eight directions got a lot of love, both the old stuff, and the new stuff, and it's all just so...tasty.<br /> <br /> Now, it doesn't feel complete because there are major cities noticeably missing an entry. Easy example is Great Forks. It has only a minor mention at most in other cities write-ups. The probably reason (because I don't have the line notes), is because the big write-up for Great Forks is in the Exigent book. So if you want to know /anything/ about Great Forks, you have to buy the Exigent pdf/book.<br /> <br /> It's the same for any city/town/territory mentioned in other books. Prasad, and it's capital Kamthahar, has no direct write-up in Across the 8 Directions because it has a write-up in Heirs to the Shogunate. Lookshy is missing any sort of write up, because again, it's in Heirs to the Shogunate. Any city that is mentioned in the Lunar book is, again, not directly mentioned in Across the 8 Directions.<br /> <br /> Now, I am not saying they should have copies of the full write-ups from the other books in Across the 8 Directions, but it would be nice to have a paragraph or two about them, and a mention on which book to go check for the full write-up. Yes, I am aware that to do that would mean more pages, and probably more art, to the book, and it would cost more, both in time and money. That fact does not change the fact that it feels like it is missing these things, that it's not quite complete.<br /> <br /> I would also really like the complete map of all eight maps stitched together, but that's a me thing.<br /> <br /> Another thing I would have liked is more of an idea for the various non-human sentients running around. Like the dragon kings, the surians. The turtle people. Beastfolk are sort of covered in Lunars I think, the panda spotted pigmy people from the south (goes to find name)..the Djala (who aren't mentioned even once in the entire book!).<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, I will again, say, this is a great book if you want to know about the diverse cultures and their practices in Creation. The art is neat, the maps are good. It's everything I wanted, and more, but I feel it's still noticeably missing a couple of things. It's well worth the price, I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27754-chandramagic","user":"ChandraMagic","date":". 01-13-2024, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27754-chandramagic","name":"ChandraMagic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T04:21:49-08:00","id":1528536,"title":"","content":"Still getting through the book in chunks, but I <i>really</i> appreciate the write-up for the Hundred Kingdoms and a breakdown on not only how to make kingdoms and republics of your own in the region but also how to give them greater detail and historical context - also really fond of the section at the end of the book discussing the supernatural elements of Creation and how often they can, do, and should interact with the mundane elements in chronicles. These feel like nice and thorough extensions of similar sections in Exalted: Essence, adding extra meat without making them entirely redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T18:02:36-08:00","id":1528966,"title":"","content":"After two editions worth of descriptions of Great Forks, I really don't need to read a 3rd rendition of it. Glad to hear it's high quality I'm waiting for a hardcover release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T05:10:11-08:00","id":1528998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1528415-across-the-eight-directions-thread?p=1528966#post1528966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After two editions worth of descriptions of Great Forks, I really don't need to read a 3rd rendition of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great Forks is in Exigents anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T21:34:34-08:00","id":1529066,"title":"","content":"I am growing more and more in favour of Creation 3rd edition map overlay. Add all the pins per book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T02:28:36-08:00","id":1529079,"title":"","content":"I must say that I like the Northeast much more than I expected to- Fray's writeup is really cool, and the idea of a whole region just sitting on a time bomb i really interesting imp. The Northwest is still my favorite region, as it is so desolated and weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T16:33:21-08:00","id":1529990,"title":"","content":"I still haven't gotten a chance to get the book, but I've seen references elsewhere to a few events and eras that seem relatively important. I hope that it isn't bad form to ask about.<br /> <br /> First, am I right to assume that the unseasonably cold &quot;little iceage&quot; from 650-660 is the Ten Years Winter mentioned in passing in an artifact description? Sort of a Game of Thrones, fimbulwinter esque event that was around the time when the Realm desperately conquered Fajad and made overtures to Wu Jian to get resources.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Second Contagion I've seen a couple of times. I assume its sort of like how the Black Death wasn't a one and done situation, but was it widespread? Did it strike at different times across Creation?<br /> <br /> Since my setting is Rajtul Island as a stand-in for a more anglo-european medieval fantasy take on Exalted, I am very interested in hearing a taste. The little ice age and the black death were very flavorful parts of real world history, and I coincidentally already had some major social changes occuring in 650-660 that I can blame on the cold and famine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T20:41:15-08:00","id":1530002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1528415-across-the-eight-directions-thread?p=1529990#post1529990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...<br /> <br /> First, am I right to assume that the unseasonably cold &quot;little iceage&quot; from 650-660 is the Ten Years Winter mentioned in passing in an artifact description? Sort of a Game of Thrones, fimbulwinter esque event that was around the time when the Realm desperately conquered Fajad and made overtures to Wu Jian to get resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. The Ten-Year Winter is only described in context if I remember right of the direlance Tusk of Galaech-Ma. And in that description it was from many centuries ago. It was the cause of a behemoth of some sort that a Lunar killed. My understanding is Fajad's conquest and Wu-Jian's own domination were just similarly-timed events. I kind of think that Fajad in fact would have not been targeted after the Wu-Jian conquest since like...it competes. It's more one hand not knowing what the other is doing. I think it is more that someone saw the weakness of the North in general as an opportunity to conquer a polity that has been of interest for a while as the Realm started turning its attention Westward. It, Wu-Jian, and Goldenseal feel like the Realm kind of trying to secure the major routes and in and out, but settling on Wu-Jian.<br /> <br /> I don't even think it is that supernaturally bad a winter. We have events like that on Earth, like the Year Without Summer, or the various events during our Little Ice Age in the 2nd Millennium CE, and times where the weather just kind of goes bad a few years in a row. It caused famines in the North and on the Isle, but like the Little Ice Age seems to be regional to those areas. The other Directions seemed to do fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1528415-across-the-eight-directions-thread?p=1529990#post1529990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Secondly, the Second Contagion I've seen a couple of times. I assume its sort of like how the Black Death wasn't a one and done situation, but was it widespread? Did it strike at different times across Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a general descriptor of how there have been waves of pandemics and plagues throughout the Northeast in the early 3rd Century. It more or less up-ended many early Realm conquests there, and destroyed a grip of Shogunate Successor States and empires. This has stymied the Realm's expansion in that Direction, as well as generally destroyed the ability of many major polities to arise there. It's an event kind of part of the Silver River Basin and Northeast general's character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1528415-across-the-eight-directions-thread?p=1529990#post1529990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since my setting is Rajtul Island as a stand-in for a more anglo-european medieval fantasy take on Exalted, I am very interested in hearing a taste. The little ice age and the black death were very flavorful parts of real world history, and I coincidentally already had some major social changes occuring in 650-660 that I can blame on the cold and famine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Contagion didn't likely go there. But if you want to add in the issues iwth climate and its impact on the island, that seems like a good way to go. It just probably is more like historical stuff than the Ten-Year Winter, which again, we don't know about but seems more the event of some bigass behemoth. And notably not all the Eras listed are like, global. Some are local events too, so something noted centuries in the North might all be forgotten in other parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T22:01:36-08:00","id":1530006,"title":"","content":"Very good point about the Ten Year Winter. I remember my previous theory was that it was a Shogunate event following the Autumn's End Incursion, but since the &quot;little ice age&quot; was listed as ten years long, my mind made a jump there. Still a nice poetic name for the event, perhaps Ill keep it. I can just say the kingdom on Rajtul, having lost track of Shogunate history mostly anyway, just coincidentally came up with the same name because it sounds cool. Or perhaps I'll go with them calling it the Fimbulwinter, to match the pseudo-norse vibes I was giving to the Rajtali sailors and pirates in the area. Either way, I really like that as a historical event. Gives a good shakeup of things, and is a good excuse for my Kingdom to go through a rough patch.<br /> <br /> And yeah, its good to know that about the Second Contagion, thank you. It sounds like a really juicy hook. Glad to know it was a localized thing. If I want to play with the idea, it could be a separate outbreak of Rajtali's own--2e had a lost dragon-king hospital on Lakshadi that I kept, so if I really want a version of the second contagion, I can blame that, and stick it anywhere on the timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T20:52:02-08:00","id":1530705,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28323-leostehr","name":"LeoStehr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T15:06:53-07:00","id":1534511,"title":"","content":"Has anyone else noticed that there are a bunch of &quot;repeated&quot; ideas in some Northern locales?<br /> <br /> The Nail of Truth of Pneuma y very similar to the tower in Fajad (the Needle). The former has this legend about Mela using it to crush a Anathema, while the latter seems to be pinning down a behemoth. I kept confusing this two places at first.<br /> <br /> The Nail of Truth I think is also above an Anathema prison... whereas Fortitude used to be a First Age prison.<br /> <br /> Then there's all this theme of &quot;underground horrors&quot; apparently everywhere: Behemoth under Fajad, Uluiru's Incarna, Vodak under Gethamane, the thing under the Silverswept plains, the Anathema prison under Pneuma, the underground cult leader in Fortitude, etc... (I haven't read about Diamond Hearth yet, but it wouldn't surprise me if there's an undescribable horror under it as well).<br /> <br /> Maybe the North fell from the sky and that's why there's so much shit under it.. (hey... sounds interesting huh...), or maybe the writers kept chatting about their ideas and never agreed who would write the &quot;underground horror city&quot; and they all submited one. I don't know...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 04-20-2024, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T17:48:40-07:00","id":1534513,"title":"","content":"Writing an underground horror city is a primary temptation in writing for a pulp swords and sorcery revival game. I suspect that many people who wrote any fan material for Exalted probably made one back in the day; I know I did (though I eventually decided to give that concept breathing room, for all that matters now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T12:23:07-07:00","id":1534529,"title":"","content":"Exalted has had a lot of scary stuff underground since at least as far back as the introduction of the Mountain Folk. Part of the premise of the Primordials for a while has been that they periodically got bored with their creations and then would shove them away out of sight, as a basis for the setting to have this kind of primeval lost world hollow Earth vibe for people that wanted to engage with it.<br /> <br /> And Third Edition seems to have opted to a large degree to go with the idea of &quot;a lot of the shit that the Primordials made was actually a lot scarier than them, and the Exalted of the First Age didn't deal with all of it (assuming that some of how they dealt with it wasn't already just also stuffing it underground&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it prevails in the North, that might just be because the North is where you get a lot of the kinds of mountains that lead into caves that lead into the underground. It's the Misty Mountains writ large, providing access to the nameless things that gnaw at the roots of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T13:00:55-07:00","id":1534530,"title":"","content":"Core book description of Gethamane, really. The section on it in Scavenger Sons elaborated on it with an unnerving account of getting lost, meeting a monster that offered to lead them back up to the surface, and paying the price of an eye (which we're told didn't even bleed that much!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}